# Built-in annotations

Doesn't change behaviour on its own; the compiler or a tool reads it.

## The compiler-facing set

- **`@Override`** — verifies you really override; **put it on every override**
- **`@Deprecated`** — warns callers; `@Deprecated(since="21", forRemoval=true)`
- **`@SuppressWarnings("unchecked")`** — silence a warning you understand — narrowest scope
- **`@FunctionalInterface`** — exactly one abstract method (module 06)

## What it is underneath

- Declared with `@interface`; **`@Target`** = where, **`@Retention`** = how long
- `SOURCE` · `CLASS` · **`RUNTIME`** — readable via **reflection** → powers `@Test`, `@Entity` (module 10)

## Carrying data

```java
@Test(timeout = 500)   // named element; arrays: {"unchecked", "deprecation"}
```
